  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="a4bb-24a6-dcea-9c6f" name="New Kingdom Egyptian (Chariot Wars) - List Notes" publicationId="513c-2d0a-024a-da5a" hidden="false">
      <description>NEW KINGDOM EGYPTIAN ARMY LIST (Chariot Wars, pp.12-18), 1600 BC to 800 BC.
Characters up to 25%; at least one character to command. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. Infantry at least 25%. Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 25%. A small army of 1,000 points can be commanded by a Brigade Commander (Hery Pedjet) rather than a General (Pharaoh, Prince, Viceroy or Imyr-Mesha).
Chariot Runners: up to one unit per unit of Chariots (an earlier-period army without chariots may use them as Egyptian javelinmen).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[New Kingdom Egyptian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry &amp; Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Standard composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
